  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Specific Contract - DIGITTMII-029299-DIGITTMII-016688-EXT-02</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Specific Contract - DIGITTMII-029299-DIGITTMII-016688-EXT-02 - The proposed Action will provide necessary highly specialised expertise for the Commission. The sector &#xbf;digital transformation&#xbf; is relatively new and the Commission continues to build and deepen in-house expertise.  At the same time, with &#xbf;digital&#xbf; being one of the focus areas of Global Gateway and in view of the necessary scale-up of Global Gateway, a substantial amount of highly specialised expertise is required immediately. The proposed action will hence complement the available in-house expertise through the involvement of external experts in very specific digital areas to ensure the proper deployment and implementation of digital partnerships aligned with EU interests. It aims to enable the sound implementation of the Global Challenges (Prosperity) Thematic Programme in digital transformation specifically, including achievement of its expected objectives and results.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;This action will cover expenditures associated with the identification, preparation, implementation, follow up, monitoring and evaluation of activities within HQ related to Global Europe/NDICI programmes in digital transformation.&amp;nbsp; This support complements existing technical assistance facilities which cannot cover for the continuous need of expertise which starts before identification, extends beyond formulation and requires continuity.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Digital Support Mechanisms will be utilised to strengthen the continuation of activities of the &#xbf;Digital Transformation&#xbf; Unit (INTPA F5) and the digital team of the &#xbf;Regional programmes for Latin America and the Caribbean&#xbf; Unit (INTPA B1) in specific digital domains, e.g. cybersecurity, e-governance, digital infrastructure, connectivity (satellite and cable), Earth observation, and Artificial Intelligence. The action aims to ensure the Unit&#xbf;s capacity to reach its goals as per the Global Gateway objectives in Digital, focusing on promoting EU interest, working with private sector and overall advancing international digital partnerships.&amp;nbsp;</narrative>
  </description>
